work_units.notes:
Build a checklist that maps every PR #246 finding to:
  - source screenshot filenames;
  - remediating TODO ID;
  - route;
  - viewport;
  - expected visual/interaction/data outcome;
  - automated and manual verification evidence.

The matrix should explicitly include the full baseline screenshot set
from this TODO.

For every audited route, cold-load with the fixture-backed server and
capture:
  - requested URL and final URL;
  - title and H1;
  - console errors/warnings;
  - non-2xx network failures;
  - raw internal error visibility;
  - app loaded state.

No route can pass this gate with visible `Binder Error`, stack trace,
undefined ID, blank loaded state, or unexpected console error.

Recapture all routes at 390px, 768px, 1280px, and 1600px where practical,
plus the focused states from PR #246:
  - Home times/ranks/speedup;
  - TPC-H matrix/list/high-contrast;
  - Star Schema/SSB;
  - DuckDB and DataFusion platform pages;
  - Result Detail chart section;
  - same-cohort Compare;
  - mixed-scale Compare;
  - Query Workbench and mobile filter drawer.

Store raw after screenshots in CI artifacts, `/tmp`, or
`BENCHBOX_OUTPUT_DIR`, then summarize the route/viewport matrix, checked
SHA, PASS/FAIL result, and any relevant manifest counts in the final audit.
Do not commit the screenshot batch.

Create `_project/audits/results-explorer-pr246-remediation-final-<date>.md`
with:
  - verdict: ready, partially ready, or not ready;
  - route and viewport matrix;
  - screenshot index;
  - console/network summary;
  - finding-by-finding closure table;
  - residual defects with severity and TODO owner;
  - explicit statement that PR #246 screenshots were used as baseline.
